# Development TLS material from scripts/gen-certs.sh (R6.3/R6.4). Never commit
# private keys, not even throwaway ones — a committed key is a key that gets
# copied into something real.
certs/

# A compiled kvbench got committed once: `go build ./...` with the source
# bind-mounted writes the binary into the module root, and `git add -A` took it.
# 7.9 MiB of build output, and the reason a push failed with HTTP 400.
bench/kvbench
cpp-app/fuzz-build/
cpp-app/build-fuzz/

# libFuzzer writes newly interesting inputs into its FIRST corpus argument. The
# documented commands now point that at /tmp, but ignore the conventional local
# name too so an ad-hoc run cannot re-add hundreds of hash-named files.
cpp-app/fuzz/corpus-generated/
